                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of state, Madrid, to Spanish minister at
                        Washington.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">(Received 4.10 p.m., November 23, 1873.)</p>
                <p>Contradict report in reference to hostile manifestations against the American
                    minister. General Sickles is treated with consideration and respect.</p>
                <p>Some intemperance of language, but the monarchical press was promptly silenced by
                    the threat of immediate punishment.</p>
                <p>The minister of the colonies reports from Havana that the restoration of
                    embargoed property to American citizens is diligently proceeded with.</p>
            </div>
